# TED-talks — DIRECT dependencies (intent). Edit this file, not requirements.txt.
#
# requirements.txt is the generated LOCKFILE: fully pinned, including transitive
# packages, targeting the Railway deploy environment (py3.11 / linux per runtime.txt).
# Railway runs `pip install -r requirements.txt` in ITS OWN builder, which has none
# of the local hardening in ~/.config/{uv/uv.toml,pip/pip.conf} — so pinning here is
# the only thing standing between a redeploy and a freshly-resolved dependency tree.
#
# Regenerate after editing (from this directory):
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --python-version 3.11 --python-platform linux \
#     -o requirements.txt
# uv applies the global 7-day cooldown (~/.config/uv/uv.toml), so the pins it
# produces are never a just-published version.
#
# Added 2026-09-02. See Code/package-vetting-checklist.md §0.

